**No, not on a draft.** Under our guidance, a cask can only leave bond for export under duty suspension once two things have happened:

1. The export declaration has been accepted.
2. The electronic movement document has been submitted and validated.

A draft EMCS document doesn't meet that requirement, so the cask stays in bond until the document is validated.

